A||||21||MinnGreenGT||"G-Series" Fiero for sale...||||4||
Z||000000||MinnGreenGT||10-09-2001||12:58 PM||||A few weeks ago, someone came up with a link to a partially completed Fiero kit-car, the "G-Series" Fiero.  I emailed the owner requesting futher info on the kit and it's current state- and this is what I sent & recieved.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>From: Rob C. Bartlett<BR>To: info@punchwerks.com<BR>Sent: 18/09/2001 9:59 AM<BR>Subject: Fiero rebody?<P>Punchwerks-<P>Ran across your website... I like the Fiero kit.  As to your statement about the Fiero aftermarket drying up- check out Pennock's Fiero Forum at <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl</A>   (that's where someone referenced your site).  What<BR>is the current fate of your G-Series kit for the Fiero?  I think people would be interested in a unique rebody instead of just regular Ferrari & Lambo ripoffs.  Do you have any further info?<P>Later!<BR>Rob Bartlett<BR>MinnGreenGT (on PFF)<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>To which I recieved this response and photos:<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>From: Greg Henderson &lt;gwh@globalserve.net&gt;<BR>Date: Wed, 19 Sep 2001 23:26:39 -0400<BR>To: &lt;rob@xtralite.com&gt;<BR>Subject: G Series Fiero<P>Hi Rob,<BR>Don't get me wrong about my "dried up Fiero market" line.  I know the kit car thing is still going and when I started this project I figured I could catch the end of that boom with 'like you say' "something other than the<BR>regular Ferrari & Lambo ripoffs".  The problem now is that it still requires more development and then a lot of marketing before it could see a return and Fiero's seem to be entering that stage of restoration rather than customization. I'm now focusing everything on the VW which is a much simpler kit.<P>Attached are a few photos of the plugs loosely hung on the car.  Moulds were completed with the exception of the tilt nose and the sail panel.  I'd be willing to sell the lot and I know it's not worth anything near what has gone into it, which makes setting a price rather difficult.  This is not a rip from any other existing kits.  The entire form was produced mostly from wood for the 'plug' stage, and moulds were then pulled.  If you'd like I can send pics of the moulds.  They're packed away in the loft.  Give me your thoughts as this thing is on it's way to becoming a retirement project as a one-off for me.<P>Greg Henderson<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gfiero01.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gfiero02.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gfiero03.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gfiero04.jpg"> <P>Anyone want to pick up a new kit car project?  I'd be willing to help with the graphics end of the marketing if anyone wants to take the fiberglass side!<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||4
