Z||000012||mrfixit58||10-09-2001||04:21 PM||||Wow! I think the kit looks great. But, I think the front end of the car is too high. The front end is definately Chrysler. The front turn signals look like the Sebring. I like the front fender vents but miss the cold air intake on the rear quarter. Where is the gas filler and the rear deck lid vents?<P>I wonder what it would look like with some side scoops? If the rear valence were continuous, you could lose the lower portion of the trunk and bring out four exhaust tips in the center like the C5 Vetts. I'd also like to see a wider rear quarter for wider tires like the Porches and maybe sholder scoops like the old Mach I Mushtangs.<P>It's really hard to pass judgement without a proper paint job. I would love to see the a finished car with 17" or 18" wheels and lower front rake.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||14
